2	//   "Let me mark an invoice as paid. Keep a record every time I do so I can check back later."
3	//
4	// On a project's detail page each invoice shows its payment status (invoice-status) and, while it is
5	// still unpaid, a control to mark it paid (invoice-pay-<id>). Marking an invoice paid flips its
6	// status to paid, survives a fresh load from the server, and — because the request wants a record
7	// kept EVERY time — appends exactly one audit record `INVOICE_PAID id=<id> amount=<amount>` per
8	// marking. Marking one invoice must not touch its siblings.
9	//
10	// Asserts ONLY through the two public channels: the UI (data-testid) and the audit file
11	// (auditLines()). Data is arranged via resetAndSeed (the app's /__test__ endpoint): `clients`
12	// honours { id, name, email }, `projects` honours { id, name, clientId } and `invoices` honours
13	// { id, amount, projectId, status }.
